In `refundDue`, the fee is now worked out on what was paid as before, taken off, and the refund rate is applied to the remainder. The minimum-refund check is made on that final amount. I also added a guard so that if the fee is at least what was paid, it returns 0 rather than passing a zero or negative amount to `share`.

I couldn't see `share` or `refundRate`, so I assumed `share` drops part of a penny the way you described. I didn't run anything, but your example (40000 paid, fee 2500, half back) should give 18750.
